# selftest.lint -- the identifier-comparison lint run against its own fixtures.
#
# identity.lint freezes the tree, so it can only ever say "nothing changed".
# That makes it a poor witness for the scanner: a scanner that reported
# nothing at all would pass it, and so would one whose string-literal
# exemption or `case-lint:` escape hatch had stopped working, because those
# only ever remove reports and the frozen set was built by the same code.
#
# This spec points the same driver at two fixtures instead.  Every comparison
# in selftest/flagged.c is in selftest.baseline and every comparison in
# selftest/silent.c is absent from it, so the two failure directions the
# driver already has become the two REDs:
#
#   a detector that stops seeing a raw comparison  -> "no longer in the tree"
#   a literal or an annotation that stops exempting -> "unclassified comparison"
#
# The fixtures are never compiled and are not in any _SOURCES.

root tests/lint/selftest

baseline selftest.baseline

marker case-lint:

comparators strcmp strncmp strcasecmp strncasecmp cieq cieqn eq eqc cistrstr strstr eq_substr
